1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,020
"Not Yours"

2
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
(Episode 9)

3
00:01:05,439 --> 00:01:05,719
Here.

4
00:01:05,799 --> 00:01:06,799
Have some water.

5
00:01:07,879 --> 00:01:09,040
Thank you.

6
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,400
Thank goodness you made it just in time.

7
00:01:12,159 --> 00:01:13,879
Are you wondering

8
00:01:13,959 --> 00:01:15,519
why I'm the one who came to rescue you,

9
00:01:16,319 --> 00:01:17,400
and not P'Eng?

10
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,159
Who the hell are you?

11
00:01:48,239 --> 00:01:50,039
How dare you barge in
here and start trouble?

12
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,325
You've been through a lot,
little brother Pao Bei.

13
00:02:07,599 --> 00:02:08,920
Master P'Aya.

14
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,600
Thank you.

15
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,759
So you still remember me!

16
00:02:40,719 --> 00:02:42,600
How did you cross these guys

17
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,040
to make them kidnap you like this?

18
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:47,200
I don't recall ever crossing them.

19
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,520
I think they got the wrong guy.

20
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:51,439
If you're looking for that celebrity,

21
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:54,159
hate to break it to you, I'm not him.

22
00:02:58,319 --> 00:02:59,319
Didn't you freakin' say

23
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:02,199
this was that celebrity
named Milan or whatever?

24
00:03:05,599 --> 00:03:07,839
He's wearing the exact
same clothes as in the photo!

25
00:03:07,919 --> 00:03:11,039
Plus, I even saw him
taking pictures with fans!

26
00:03:25,719 --> 00:03:26,959
Damn you!

27
00:03:27,039 --> 00:03:28,760
All you ever do is stir up trouble for me!

28
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,239
Damn it!

29
00:03:30,319 --> 00:03:31,679
That Milan they're talking about

30
00:03:31,759 --> 00:03:33,279
is the celebrity staying at the house.

31
00:03:35,439 --> 00:03:36,239
A misunderstanding!

32
00:03:36,319 --> 00:03:37,536
It's all a big misunderstanding!

33
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,679
We're so sorry.

34
00:03:38,759 --> 00:03:40,280
We apologize to you both.

35
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,239
Sorry!

36
00:03:43,319 --> 00:03:45,599
So sorry!

37
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:48,359
Oh, right.

38
00:03:48,439 --> 00:03:51,479
That Milan you mentioned? He's with me too.

39
00:03:52,879 --> 00:03:54,079
Even though P'Eng didn't come,

40
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,719
you really have him to thank.

41
00:03:56,599 --> 00:03:58,920
If he hadn't accused me of kidnapping you,

42
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,520
I wouldn't have even known about this.

43
00:04:01,919 --> 00:04:03,799
You know P'Eng's temper.

44
00:04:03,879 --> 00:04:05,039
He's a real hothead.

45
00:04:05,759 --> 00:04:07,599
I was worried he might
provoke the kidnappers,

46
00:04:07,879 --> 00:04:10,679
so I quietly tracked down
the van they took you in,

47
00:04:10,759 --> 00:04:12,199
and finally found you.

48
00:04:13,639 --> 00:04:17,160
So this was your first
time meeting these guys?

49
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,120
Of course.

50
00:04:19,166 --> 00:04:22,480
Did you think I was in league with
them and actually wanted to kidnap you?

51
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:24,800
No, not at all.

52
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,560
So that means

53
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,240
the "boss" they mentioned
isn't Master P'Aya.

54
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,920
Then the person they said kidnapped Mom

55
00:04:33,266 --> 00:04:34,321
could very well be...

56
00:04:34,346 --> 00:04:35,286
P'Eng.

57
00:04:35,639 --> 00:04:36,839
But why on earth would he do that?

58
00:04:36,879 --> 00:04:39,520
Even though I'm not entirely on
board with you dating P'Eng,

59
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:41,120
I'd never stoop so low though.

60
00:04:49,759 --> 00:04:51,279
I know P'Eng all too well.

61
00:04:51,879 --> 00:04:53,680
When he first gets together with a person,

62
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,999
he falls head over heels,

63
00:04:56,023 --> 00:04:57,023
loves like crazy,

64
00:04:57,759 --> 00:04:59,000
willing to give the world.

65
00:04:59,519 --> 00:05:01,479
He makes you feel like
the luckiest person alive,

66
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:02,680
just like right now.

67
00:05:04,319 --> 00:05:05,800
Once he falls out of love,

68
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,080
you'll end up just like these toys,

69
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,759
tossed aside.

70
00:05:10,319 --> 00:05:12,400
Lovers, friends, it makes no difference.

71
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:14,720
Everyone is disposable to him.

72
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,160
Easily replaced at any moment.

73
00:05:17,519 --> 00:05:18,519
Or,

74
00:05:19,199 --> 00:05:21,160
he'll retreat into the shadows,

75
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,200
and find other ways to drive you crazy

76
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,160
until you're desperate to run,

77
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,879
before dumping you for good.

78
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:31,960
See?

79
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,439
Just like this toy car.

80
00:05:33,519 --> 00:05:35,439
He only played with it once or twice,

81
00:05:35,519 --> 00:05:36,599
and never touched it again.

82
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:39,079
I kept them all safe for him,

83
00:05:39,639 --> 00:05:41,519
just in case he ever
remembers them one day.

84
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,160
Even though my little
brother gives me a hard time,

85
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,720
my heart still aches for him,

86
00:05:50,519 --> 00:05:51,839
and I truly want him to be happy.

87
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:06,920
Of course,

88
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,359
I'm only saying this
based on his track record,

89
00:06:10,439 --> 00:06:12,000
just to give you a heads-up.

90
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:14,359
After all, you're innocent in all this.

91
00:06:14,439 --> 00:06:16,240
I don't want to see you get hurt.

92
00:06:18,319 --> 00:06:20,480
I want P'Eng to settle down with someone

93
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,800
for the long haul, too.

94
00:06:22,879 --> 00:06:24,720
For a guy like my brother, though,

95
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,160
that's asking way too much.

96
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:28,240
Sometimes even I don't know what he wants.

97
00:06:29,839 --> 00:06:31,119
Anyway,

98
00:06:31,199 --> 00:06:33,559
if you're really serious about
making things work with him,

99
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,920
you have my blessing.

100
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:41,240
I feel like I'm not good
enough for him right now.

101
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,240
I hope that one day,

102
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,920
I can stand tall beside
him and truly have his back.

103
00:06:49,839 --> 00:06:51,160
If you ever need a hand,

104
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,360
my door is always open.

105
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:54,720
Thank you, Master P'Aya.

106
00:06:55,439 --> 00:06:57,240
Your family has already
done so much for me.

107
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,520
Especially letting that whole
thing with the pricey ring slide...

108
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:01,840
Ring?

109
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:02,920
What ring?

110
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,120
Oh, nothing.

111
00:07:09,519 --> 00:07:10,559
Ah, I get it.

112
00:07:10,639 --> 00:07:13,279
Is he making you wear
matching diamond rings again?

113
00:07:14,079 --> 00:07:17,399
That kid pulls the exact same
move every time he dates.

114
00:07:18,079 --> 00:07:19,720
He actually doesn't know about the ring?

115
00:07:20,519 --> 00:07:22,456
Something that valuable
went missing from the house,

116
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,839
and Master P'Aya has no clue?

117
00:07:24,519 --> 00:07:25,639
If...

118
00:07:26,959 --> 00:07:29,119
If P'Eng really is the one
who kidnapped Mom,

119
00:07:29,199 --> 00:07:30,519
could the stolen ring

120
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,879
have been staged by him too?

121
00:07:32,959 --> 00:07:34,399
Why would he go to such lengths?

122
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,160
Everything is such a mess.

123
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:41,319
Actually, tonight he was supposed to
attend an emergency board meeting with me.

124
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:42,439
Except he was a no-show.

125
00:07:43,279 --> 00:07:44,519
I only found out later

126
00:07:45,639 --> 00:07:46,799
that he went looking for you.

127
00:07:47,519 --> 00:07:48,080
Will...

128
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:48,879
Will that cause any trouble for him?

129
00:07:48,959 --> 00:07:50,520
The trouble is,

130
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:53,920
this meeting had his
voting rights on the line.

131
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,319
If he loses them...

132
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,439
Never mind.

133
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:58,919
You don't need to worry about that.

134
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:00,839
All you need to know

135
00:08:01,639 --> 00:08:03,679
is that the price P'Eng paid for you

136
00:08:03,759 --> 00:08:05,600
is far greater than you could ever imagine.

137
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,000
What price?

138
00:08:08,839 --> 00:08:10,439
Before our father passed away,

139
00:08:10,519 --> 00:08:11,759
he put a clause in his will:

140
00:08:12,759 --> 00:08:14,879
during P'Eng's time at the company,

141
00:08:14,959 --> 00:08:16,920
if his personal relationships
ever get in the way

142
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,439
of company decisions,

143
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:21,600
his shares automatically transfer to me.

144
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:22,720
Granted,

145
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:24,720
that clause is almost never invoked,

146
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:27,040
yet for your sake,

147
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:28,759
he skipped tonight's meeting.

148
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,480
If that's true,

149
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:34,720
then why would he still...

150
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,760
The more I think about
it, the less sense it makes.

151
00:08:38,519 --> 00:08:39,720
My head is spinning.

152
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:47,480
Stop pacing!

153
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,199
Young Master.

154
00:08:51,279 --> 00:08:52,719
Well? Any news?

155
00:08:52,799 --> 00:08:53,599
Yes, sir.

156
00:08:53,679 --> 00:08:55,056
We tracked down the van's location,

157
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,255
though we don't know
how long it'll stay put.

158
00:08:56,279 --> 00:08:58,079
If we're going, we need to move fast.

159
00:08:58,159 --> 00:08:59,640
Good. We leave now.

160
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:00,759
I'm coming with you.

161
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:02,655
At least I know what those guys look like.

162
00:09:02,679 --> 00:09:04,375
And if things get ugly, an
extra pair of hands won't hurt.

163
00:09:04,399 --> 00:09:05,040
Right.

164
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,120
Count me in.

165
00:09:08,039 --> 00:09:08,839
Stay out of this.

166
00:09:08,919 --> 00:09:09,719
Given who you are,

167
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:10,816
you can't afford to get mixed up in this.

168
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:12,839
Fine. I'll hold down the fort here.

169
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:13,936
Just in case Pao Bei comes back,

170
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,096
someone will be here for him.

171
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,120
Let's roll.

172
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,960
Where are you all rushing off to?

173
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:23,000
None of your business.

174
00:09:27,879 --> 00:09:28,879
You...

175
00:09:29,679 --> 00:09:31,319
Pao Bei! How did you get back?

176
00:09:31,399 --> 00:09:33,599
Didn't you claim I kidnapped him?

177
00:09:33,679 --> 00:09:36,039
So I kidnapped him right back for you.

178
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,176
You're hurt! What happened?

179
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:42,520
Did they do anything else to you?

180
00:09:43,039 --> 00:09:44,280
Take me to them.

181
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,360
Now!

182
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:47,640
Don't go.

183
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:48,880
What's wrong?

184
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:50,360
I said don't go.

185
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:51,760
It's just a scratch.

186
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:53,599
Anyone who dares lay a finger on you

187
00:09:53,679 --> 00:09:54,679
is dead meat.

188
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:56,159
I told you not to go!

189
00:09:58,559 --> 00:09:59,919
You should all stay right here.

190
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,200
I wasn't their target this time.

191
00:10:04,879 --> 00:10:05,879
It was Milan.

192
00:10:06,759 --> 00:10:07,799
Milan?

193
00:10:07,879 --> 00:10:09,080
Why are they after Milan?

194
00:10:11,879 --> 00:10:13,719
From what I overheard,

195
00:10:13,799 --> 00:10:15,399
your agency's boss must be behind it.

196
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:19,000
So you guys had better

197
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:21,079
stick close to Milan
and keep an eye on him.

198
00:10:21,159 --> 00:10:22,279
I'm safe now.

199
00:10:22,919 --> 00:10:24,559
You don't have to worry about me anymore.

200
00:10:24,759 --> 00:10:26,159
As for your clothes,

201
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:28,519
I'll wash them and get them back to you.

202
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:32,120
Watch your back for the next little while.

203
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,000
Please stay safe.

204
00:10:53,679 --> 00:10:54,760
I'm changing.

205
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:55,960
Could you please step out?

206
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:58,480
What on earth did he say to you?

207
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,480
I don't know who you're talking about.

208
00:11:04,159 --> 00:11:05,280
I'm talking about P'Aya.

209
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,799
What did he say

210
00:11:06,879 --> 00:11:08,479
to make you act like this?

211
00:11:08,559 --> 00:11:09,936
Are you going to treat me like this again?

212
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,600
I asked you a question. Answer me!

213
00:11:12,559 --> 00:11:14,319
Was it P'Aya

214
00:11:14,399 --> 00:11:15,400
who made me like this?

215
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:16,919
Wasn't it you, Master P'Eng?

216
00:11:17,559 --> 00:11:18,880
What did I do?

217
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:20,640
What nonsense are you talking about?

218
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:21,920
You know exactly what you did.

219
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:23,920
Enough.

220
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,400
I don't want to talk anymore today.

221
00:11:31,279 --> 00:11:32,400
What is this?

222
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:34,120
Why do you have his stuff?

223
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,279
Let go!

224
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:38,079
Open your eyes and take a good look.

225
00:11:38,159 --> 00:11:39,360
Look at what it's for.

226
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,799
This is a wound. It's bleeding.

227
00:11:40,879 --> 00:11:41,799
This handkerchief is to stop the bleeding.

228
00:11:41,879 --> 00:11:43,159
Need me to spell it out for you?

229
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:45,840
Stop the bleeding...

230
00:11:47,679 --> 00:11:48,960
Let me wrap it up for you.

231
00:11:50,919 --> 00:11:52,360
What did you promise me?

232
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:53,440
Do you even remember?

233
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,096
Why are you refusing to listen again

234
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,120
and losing your mind?

235
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:00,015
How am I supposed to be with you like this?

236
00:12:00,039 --> 00:12:01,080
I'm exhausted.

237
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,600
Do you really love me?

238
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:09,440
Your brother really knows you well, though.

239
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,920
I'm warning you.

240
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,559
Don't compare me to him.

241
00:12:16,639 --> 00:12:18,120
I don't want to fight with you today.

242
00:12:18,759 --> 00:12:19,439
I'm too tired.

243
00:12:19,519 --> 00:12:20,519
Don't go!

244
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,960
Nobody's leaving until we clear this up!

245
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:25,600
Enough!

246
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,200
We're getting nowhere today.

247
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,479
Then say you love me.

248
00:12:30,559 --> 00:12:32,015
Say you love me, and I'll let you go.

249
00:12:32,039 --> 00:12:33,840
Just say it, and I'll let you leave, okay?

250
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,680
What's the point of doing this?

251
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:36,360
Grow up!

252
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,000
Say you love me!

253
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:38,160
Say you love me!

254
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,559
Say it!

255
00:12:39,639 --> 00:12:40,199
Say you love me!

256
00:12:40,279 --> 00:12:41,416
Say you love me and I'll let you go,

257
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:43,080
please?

258
00:12:43,639 --> 00:12:44,360
I can't love you when you're like this.

259
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,040
Say you love me!

260
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:46,240
Say it!

261
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:49,880
Get off me!

262
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:50,960
Are you out of your mind?

263
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:53,679
This is exactly why

264
00:12:53,759 --> 00:12:54,759
I can't love you!

265
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,279
Say you love me!

266
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,600
Have you lost your mind?

267
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:40,279
You disgust me.

268
00:13:50,879 --> 00:13:51,879
Are you okay?

269
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,080
You need to get that
wound treated properly.

270
00:13:56,279 --> 00:13:57,640
I'm fine.

271
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,480
I'll take care of it
myself when I get home.

272
00:14:01,039 --> 00:14:02,399
Your clothes got dirty.

273
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:05,959
That outfit meant so much,

274
00:14:06,039 --> 00:14:07,439
and now it's ruined.

275
00:14:07,519 --> 00:14:08,600
I'm really sorry.

276
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:10,479
Don't be silly.

277
00:14:10,559 --> 00:14:11,719
It's just clothes.

278
00:14:11,799 --> 00:14:13,160
Don't worry about it.

279
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,360
All that matters is that you're safe.

280
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,519
Besides,

281
00:14:17,279 --> 00:14:19,759
this is partly my fault.

282
00:14:21,039 --> 00:14:22,040
Don't say that.

283
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,200
None of this is your fault.

284
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:24,240
Don't blame yourself.

285
00:14:24,759 --> 00:14:26,120
See? I'm totally fine.

286
00:14:26,679 --> 00:14:27,959
People say I'm tough,

287
00:14:28,039 --> 00:14:29,360
and luck is always on my side.

288
00:14:30,799 --> 00:14:31,799
Heading back?

289
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:34,480
Why don't you stay here tonight?

290
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,320
I'm tired.

291
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:38,919
I want to go home.

292
00:14:39,639 --> 00:14:40,639
Let's go, then.

293
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,640
No need.

294
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:44,679
You should stay here with Milan tonight.

295
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,640
Then I'll have a car take you home.

296
00:14:49,399 --> 00:14:50,799
Master P'Aya,

297
00:14:50,879 --> 00:14:52,480
let me drive Pao Bei home.

298
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,520
You've had a long day yourself.

299
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,600
You should get some rest.

300
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,480
Thanks for the trouble, Mingkun.

301
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,360
Mingkun,

302
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:05,759
I rode the scooter he gave me here today.

303
00:15:06,759 --> 00:15:08,279
It looks like it's going to rain.

304
00:15:08,919 --> 00:15:10,319
Could you move it under the shed

305
00:15:10,399 --> 00:15:11,399
so it doesn't get wet?

306
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:13,240
Don't worry, it's all taken care of.

307
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,719
It's in the greenhouse.

308
00:15:14,799 --> 00:15:15,799
Okay.

309
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:43,520
Say you love me!

310
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:44,600
Say it!

311
00:15:46,639 --> 00:15:47,639
Have you lost your mind?

312
00:15:51,879 --> 00:15:52,879
Mingkun,

313
00:15:55,759 --> 00:15:56,759
can I trust you?

314
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,360
Why do you ask all of a sudden?

315
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Honestly,

316
00:16:01,879 --> 00:16:02,880
I...

317
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:03,640
I'm exhausted.

318
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:05,240
I don't know who to trust anymore.

319
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:08,319
While I don't know exactly what happened,

320
00:16:08,399 --> 00:16:09,319
nor can I say for sure

321
00:16:09,399 --> 00:16:10,919
whether I'm trustworthy,

322
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:13,000
as a rule,

323
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:14,520
I only speak of what I know

324
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,960
or the facts I'm allowed to share.

325
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:18,720
Then,

326
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,399
can I trust P'Eng?

327
00:16:24,039 --> 00:16:25,039
Yes.

328
00:16:26,759 --> 00:16:28,360
If I'm supposed to trust him,

329
00:16:29,159 --> 00:16:31,840
why does all the damning
evidence point to him?

330
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:35,320
Was he the one who took Mom away?

331
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,480
If not,

332
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:40,120
the boss could have meant P'Aya.

333
00:16:42,159 --> 00:16:43,919
But P'Aya was the one who saved me.

334
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:47,040
And he seems so reliable.

335
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:49,080
He doesn't seem like he'd ever hurt me.

336
00:16:49,639 --> 00:16:51,240
My head hurts.

337
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,679
Everything's such a mess.

338
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:55,720
If he has to sacrifice his
stake in the company for me,

339
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:57,360
I don't want that either.

340
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,440
I can't let him lose
everything because of me.

341
00:17:04,839 --> 00:17:06,640
Congratulations on joining Yingyu Group

342
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,376
as a Product Tester in
the Product Department.

343
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:10,600
We look forward to working alongside you

344
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:11,759
toward a bright future.

345
00:17:11,839 --> 00:17:13,080
Either way,

346
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:15,080
I'll join the company
and learn the ropes first.

347
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,960
While I'm at it, I can keep an eye out

348
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:19,360
to see who's good and who's bad.

349
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:20,599
Maybe I'll find some clues.

350
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:28,920
Still,

351
00:17:29,839 --> 00:17:30,839
what about him?

352
00:17:32,519 --> 00:17:33,960
Is he doing okay?

353
00:17:47,119 --> 00:17:48,600
Say you love me!

354
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:49,360
Just say you love me!

355
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:50,640
Say it!

356
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:52,960
Say you love me!

357
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,200
Come in.

358
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:03,039
Master,

359
00:18:03,119 --> 00:18:05,319
Pao Bei is safely back home.

360
00:18:07,039 --> 00:18:08,039
Okay.

361
00:18:09,759 --> 00:18:13,000
Should we still set up
the snow scene for him?

362
00:18:17,279 --> 00:18:18,359
Cancel it.

363
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,280
It's never supposed to snow

364
00:18:25,039 --> 00:18:26,319
in Mancheng anyway.

365
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,440
Also,

366
00:18:29,279 --> 00:18:30,679
HR just

367
00:18:30,759 --> 00:18:32,800
sent Pao Bei his onboarding notice.

368
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:35,160
Should we cancel that as well?

369
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,440
Why cancel it?

370
00:18:37,599 --> 00:18:38,599
He...

371
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,519
He owes me money.

372
00:18:43,599 --> 00:18:45,399
He's not going anywhere
until he pays it off.

373
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,000
He has to work tirelessly for me

374
00:18:47,039 --> 00:18:48,119
and be at my beck and call.

375
00:18:49,039 --> 00:18:50,279
Yes, sir.

376
00:18:50,359 --> 00:18:51,599
We all work tirelessly for you,

377
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:52,720
at your beck and call.

378
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:05,279
So,

379
00:19:07,079 --> 00:19:10,200
you also think I shouldn't
have treated him like that?

380
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:12,840
I wouldn't dare blame you.

381
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:14,039
I'm used to it.

382
00:19:14,599 --> 00:19:17,199
It's just that Pao Bei

383
00:19:17,279 --> 00:19:18,839
doesn't seem used to this side of you.

384
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:21,240
If you want to get along with him,

385
00:19:21,759 --> 00:19:24,039
I'm afraid you'll really
need to work on that.

386
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,480
Got it.

387
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:29,920
By the way,

388
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:33,519
put extra guards on Milan.

389
00:19:35,039 --> 00:19:38,999
Also, find out who kidnapped Pao Bei.

390
00:19:39,079 --> 00:19:39,920
Bring him to me.

391
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,120
I'll interrogate him myself.

392
00:19:42,039 --> 00:19:43,039
Understood.

393
00:19:44,799 --> 00:19:45,679
One more thing.

394
00:19:45,759 --> 00:19:47,119
Keep a close eye on my brother.

395
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,600
Don't let him meddle in my business.

396
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:51,279
Got that?

397
00:19:51,359 --> 00:19:52,599
Got it, Master.

398
00:20:00,799 --> 00:20:02,039
In this battle,

399
00:20:04,359 --> 00:20:07,759
let's see who comes out on top.

400
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:35,960
I had no idea

401
00:20:36,759 --> 00:20:38,799
this company would be
even grander than I imagined.

402
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:41,079
It's like a whole other world.

403
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:50,240
Excuse me, are you Mr. Pao Bei?

404
00:20:50,799 --> 00:20:51,840
Yes, that's me.

405
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:52,759
It's a pleasure to meet you,

406
00:20:52,839 --> 00:20:53,719
Mr. Pao Bei.

407
00:20:53,799 --> 00:20:55,359
I'm Susan from HR.

408
00:20:56,039 --> 00:20:57,279
Nice to meet you too.

409
00:20:57,359 --> 00:20:59,439
And please, just call me Pao Bei.

410
00:20:59,519 --> 00:21:01,120
No need to be so formal.

411
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:02,439
Alright, Pao Bei.

412
00:21:02,519 --> 00:21:04,600
Let me show you to your office.

413
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:05,680
Right this way.

414
00:21:16,599 --> 00:21:17,920
Here is your office.

415
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:36,039
Susan, is there a mistake?

416
00:21:36,119 --> 00:21:36,719
I...

417
00:21:36,799 --> 00:21:38,080
I'm just a new hire.

418
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,480
Shouldn't I be sitting out there?

419
00:21:40,079 --> 00:21:41,535
It doesn't feel right
having a private room.

420
00:21:41,559 --> 00:21:42,936
This looks like an executive's office.

421
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,800
This came directly from higher up.

422
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:47,079
They told me to get you a comfortable spot.

423
00:21:48,359 --> 00:21:50,535
You really don't have to
go to all this trouble, Susan.

424
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:52,279
A regular desk out there is fine.

425
00:21:52,359 --> 00:21:55,599
An office like this is way
too much pressure for me.

426
00:21:56,799 --> 00:21:57,400
Alright.

427
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:59,119
I didn't think that through.

428
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:02,039
Why don't you rest in here for a bit?

429
00:22:02,119 --> 00:22:04,095
Once the regular meeting
wraps up, I'll double-check

430
00:22:04,119 --> 00:22:05,439
and sort out your exact seating.

431
00:22:05,519 --> 00:22:06,519
Does that work for you?

432
00:22:06,599 --> 00:22:07,759
Of course, no problem at all.

433
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,959
Honestly, I'm totally new to this.

434
00:22:11,039 --> 00:22:13,359
I'll be counting on your guidance, Susan.

435
00:22:14,440 --> 00:22:15,440
Sure thing.

436
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:17,240
Boss P'Aya.

437
00:22:18,119 --> 00:22:19,759
Boss P'Aya, about that audit report...

438
00:22:19,839 --> 00:22:20,936
If we submit it the way
Boss P'Eng wants, it might...

439
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:21,800
Save it for later.

440
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:22,880
Boss P'Aya.

441
00:22:25,759 --> 00:22:26,759
Welcome aboard.

442
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,039
I heard.

443
00:22:29,119 --> 00:22:31,160
P'Eng set you up with a private office.

444
00:22:32,359 --> 00:22:35,039
I actually just asked to
switch to a regular desk.

445
00:22:35,119 --> 00:22:37,080
As a rookie, sitting in here

446
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,400
really isn't appropriate.

447
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,039
Very sensible of you.

448
00:22:41,119 --> 00:22:43,199
P'Eng can be way too impulsive sometimes.

449
00:22:43,279 --> 00:22:45,719
He never thinks about
how things affect others.

450
00:22:45,799 --> 00:22:46,999
Just focus on your work.

451
00:22:47,079 --> 00:22:49,160
Let me know anytime if you need anything.

452
00:22:52,039 --> 00:22:54,960
Looks like the new guy is going places.

453
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:02,519
Alright.

454
00:23:02,599 --> 00:23:03,479
Team Lead Bob,

455
00:23:03,559 --> 00:23:04,400
walk us through

456
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,040
the details of our variety show project

457
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,199
so Mr. Milan here

458
00:23:08,279 --> 00:23:10,320
can get a sense of your overall pitch,

459
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:12,280
and see how we can
seamlessly blend our product

460
00:23:12,519 --> 00:23:14,840
with his persona.

461
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:15,920
Got it, Boss P'Eng.

462
00:23:18,359 --> 00:23:19,160
Everyone, take a look.

463
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:20,880
Here is my proposal for the variety show.

464
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,999
Over here, we have four main points.

465
00:23:23,079 --> 00:23:24,200
These are the key takeaways.

466
00:23:24,799 --> 00:23:27,639
These are the selling points for
integrating our product into the show.

467
00:23:27,839 --> 00:23:29,199
And during the show's segments,

468
00:23:29,279 --> 00:23:31,959
we've naturally woven in
product placement for our sauces.

469
00:23:32,039 --> 00:23:33,039
Pao Bei.

470
00:23:33,119 --> 00:23:34,119
Master P'Aya.

471
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,160
No, wait.

472
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:37,560
Hello, Boss P'Aya.

473
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:39,279
How's your first day going?

474
00:23:39,359 --> 00:23:40,839
Having any trouble settling in?

475
00:23:41,759 --> 00:23:43,839
I just got here, actually,
and the vibe seems great.

476
00:23:44,559 --> 00:23:45,575
Everyone's been really nice.

477
00:23:45,599 --> 00:23:46,599
It's just...

478
00:23:49,279 --> 00:23:50,599
Never mind, it's nothing.

479
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:53,080
Is that brat P'Eng giving
you a hard time again?

480
00:23:54,759 --> 00:23:55,199
Not at all.

481
00:23:55,279 --> 00:23:57,678
Actually, I owe him thanks
for getting me such a great job.

482
00:23:57,759 --> 00:23:59,359
And thanks to you too, Master P'Aya.

483
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:01,719
Good to hear.

484
00:24:01,799 --> 00:24:04,119
Reach out anytime if you need anything.

485
00:24:04,839 --> 00:24:05,439
Oh, right.

486
00:24:05,519 --> 00:24:06,976
We don't have each other's
contact info yet, do we?

487
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:09,039
Let's add each other
so we can stay in touch.

488
00:24:09,119 --> 00:24:10,119
Sure.

489
00:24:13,079 --> 00:24:14,959
I think I left my phone at my desk.

490
00:24:15,039 --> 00:24:16,119
Let me go grab it.

491
00:24:16,759 --> 00:24:17,759
I'll wait here.

492
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:21,320
Just a second.

493
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:23,080
I'm confident that once the show airs,

494
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:24,800
it will give our brand exposure

495
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:26,519
a massive boost.

496
00:24:27,039 --> 00:24:28,439
Look at the kid hustling.

497
00:24:28,519 --> 00:24:30,480
Running off his feet on his very first day.

498
00:24:34,720 --> 00:24:35,720
Here.

499
00:24:38,039 --> 00:24:39,239
As for the sauces,

500
00:24:39,319 --> 00:24:41,039
I designed a game segment.

501
00:24:41,119 --> 00:24:42,519
Take a look here.

502
00:24:42,599 --> 00:24:44,640
We'll tie in our new product R&amp;D as well.

503
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:46,319
When we get to the blind taste test...

504
00:24:48,880 --> 00:24:49,880
Sent you my contact.

505
00:24:50,876 --> 00:24:56,130
[A flood of office gossip about Pao Bei]

506
00:24:57,079 --> 00:24:58,920
Boss P'Aya, what's this?

507
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,000
What's wrong?

508
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:03,800
I think you sent the wrong thing.

509
00:25:06,799 --> 00:25:08,160
My bad, wrong file.

510
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:12,759
Pao Bei, just pretend you didn't see that.

511
00:25:13,279 --> 00:25:15,119
It's just mindless gossip anyway.

512
00:25:17,799 --> 00:25:19,880
Understood, Boss
P'Aya. I didn't see a thing.

513
00:25:21,319 --> 00:25:22,640
P'Eng mentioned before

514
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:24,160
that you rarely come into the office

515
00:25:24,240 --> 00:25:25,680
or get involved in company affairs.

516
00:25:26,559 --> 00:25:28,519
Running into you on my very first day...

517
00:25:28,599 --> 00:25:30,039
What a coincidence.

518
00:25:30,119 --> 00:25:31,320
Quite a coincidence indeed.

519
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:32,279
Actually,

520
00:25:32,359 --> 00:25:34,255
I wasn't even planning to
attend today's board meeting.

521
00:25:34,279 --> 00:25:36,599
Some things you just have
to keep an eye on yourself.

522
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,080
Boss P'Eng,

523
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:41,239
is there an issue with the proposal?

524
00:25:41,319 --> 00:25:42,479
Carry on.

525
00:25:42,559 --> 00:25:43,559
I'll head to the restroom.

526
00:25:46,599 --> 00:25:47,999
I should get back to work.

527
00:25:48,079 --> 00:25:48,800
Excuse me.

528
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:49,960
Go ahead.

529
00:25:53,519 --> 00:25:54,799
That screenshot just now...

530
00:25:55,440 --> 00:25:57,039
There's no way that was an accident.

531
00:26:11,759 --> 00:26:12,759
What are you up to?

532
00:26:13,880 --> 00:26:15,120
That's the question

533
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:16,519
I should be asking you.

534
00:26:17,119 --> 00:26:18,600
Why did you add him?

535
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:19,680
Who?

536
00:26:21,519 --> 00:26:22,959
You mean your brother?

537
00:26:23,039 --> 00:26:24,400
He asked to add me.

538
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:26,160
Told me to reach out if I needed anything.

539
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:27,240
Why shouldn't I?

540
00:26:28,759 --> 00:26:30,200
Because I said so.

541
00:26:31,359 --> 00:26:32,559
Because you said so?

542
00:26:33,319 --> 00:26:34,519
Who do you think you are?

543
00:26:35,232 --> 00:26:36,312
God?

544
00:26:38,759 --> 00:26:39,759
Even God

545
00:26:39,839 --> 00:26:41,559
doesn't get to control my personal freedom!

546
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:48,640
Give me your phone.

547
00:26:48,720 --> 00:26:49,320
No!

548
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:50,400
Hand it over.

549
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:51,479
Give it to me!

550
00:26:51,559 --> 00:26:52,719
No way!

551
00:26:52,799 --> 00:26:53,640
Give me the phone!

552
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:54,600
Ditch this one.

553
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,080
I'll get you a new one.

554
00:26:56,160 --> 00:26:56,600
I don't want a new one!

555
00:26:56,680 --> 00:26:57,800
I want mine!

556
00:26:57,873 --> 00:26:59,048
Do you not understand English?

557
00:26:59,079 --> 00:27:00,376
I told you I'm buying you the
latest, top-of-the-line model.

558
00:27:00,400 --> 00:27:01,400
Are you deaf?

559
00:27:01,440 --> 00:27:01,880
I don't want it!

560
00:27:01,960 --> 00:27:02,840
Give it back!

561
00:27:02,920 --> 00:27:03,920
Give it back to me!

562
00:27:17,319 --> 00:27:19,439
If I switch phones, my mom
won't be able to reach me!

563
00:27:20,160 --> 00:27:21,799
I need to get a hold of her

564
00:27:23,359 --> 00:27:25,519
so I can pay back everything I owe you.

565
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,880
I don't want to owe you anything anymore!

566
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:39,759
So you really

567
00:27:41,839 --> 00:27:43,279
don't want anything from me, huh?

568
00:27:51,359 --> 00:27:52,599
That's right. I don't need [anything].

569
00:28:01,759 --> 00:28:02,880
And another thing,

570
00:28:03,839 --> 00:28:05,440
this office isn't right for me.

571
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:07,200
I haven't earned it.

572
00:28:08,279 --> 00:28:10,439
I'll take a regular desk out
there with everyone else.

573
00:28:11,079 --> 00:28:12,759
Thanks for looking out for me, Boss P'Eng,

574
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:16,280
but please stop giving a
nobody like me special treatment.

575
00:28:34,039 --> 00:28:35,199
Alright, everyone.

576
00:28:35,279 --> 00:28:37,055
Let's kick off this week's
department meeting.

577
00:28:37,079 --> 00:28:40,000
First, let's welcome our
new team member, Pao Bei.

578
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:48,560
Let's start by following
up on our core strategy.

579
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:51,400
The first key project in our
Heritage Reimagined line:

580
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:53,800
optimizing the umami formula
for our premium oyster sauce.

581
00:28:54,759 --> 00:28:57,800
Jason, you'll spearhead the R&amp;D task force.

582
00:28:57,880 --> 00:29:00,479
The goal is to maintain
that classic savory flavor

583
00:29:00,559 --> 00:29:02,800
while cutting sodium by 30%,

584
00:29:02,880 --> 00:29:05,039
with zero compromise on taste or texture.

585
00:29:05,119 --> 00:29:06,119
That is non-negotiable.

586
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:06,959
Got it.

587
00:29:07,039 --> 00:29:10,759
Test three new yeast extract
alternatives by the end of the week.

588
00:29:10,839 --> 00:29:13,840
I want initial sensory evaluation
data on my desk by Friday,

589
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:15,600
along with a cost analysis report.

590
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:18,239
Remember, flavor is the bottom line.

591
00:29:18,319 --> 00:29:20,559
I don't want a healthy
product that tastes terrible.

592
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:24,759
Alright.

593
00:29:24,839 --> 00:29:26,359
Those are the main priorities.

594
00:29:27,119 --> 00:29:28,039
Now, Pao Bei.

595
00:29:28,119 --> 00:29:31,400
I've got a tricky assignment for you.

596
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:32,480
Think you can handle it?

597
00:29:33,279 --> 00:29:34,160
I can.

598
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:35,360
Count on me.

599
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:36,320
Good.

600
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:40,519
You'll be in sole charge
of clearing out, sorting,

601
00:29:40,599 --> 00:29:43,199
and cataloging all the failed R&amp;D samples.

602
00:29:43,279 --> 00:29:45,120
Treat them just like official products.

603
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:47,360
Create a file for every
single rejected batch

604
00:29:47,440 --> 00:29:49,239
documenting exactly why it was scrapped.

605
00:29:49,319 --> 00:29:51,799
Consider this your first lesson
in understanding our products.

606
00:29:52,119 --> 00:29:52,999
Pao Bei,

607
00:29:53,079 --> 00:29:54,999
you're sure you're up for this,

608
00:29:55,079 --> 00:29:56,160
right?

609
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:57,679
I've never done it before,

610
00:29:57,759 --> 00:29:59,239
but I'll give it everything I've got.

611
00:29:59,880 --> 00:30:00,679
Mm-hmm.

612
00:30:00,759 --> 00:30:01,759
Good.

613
00:30:02,359 --> 00:30:03,959
It's no walk in the park.

614
00:30:04,039 --> 00:30:05,039
Good luck.

615
00:30:05,799 --> 00:30:06,799
Meeting adjourned.

616
00:31:09,599 --> 00:31:10,679
You should get out of here.

617
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:13,640
You shouldn't be in a place
like this dressed like that.

618
00:31:13,960 --> 00:31:16,200
If the smell gets on your
clothes, it'll never come out.

619
00:31:17,720 --> 00:31:18,720
Do you really

620
00:31:20,759 --> 00:31:22,119
have to do this?

621
00:31:25,319 --> 00:31:26,799
I've always worked in kitchens.

622
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:29,120
This kind of work is nothing to me.

623
00:31:29,200 --> 00:31:30,480
How much longer will it take?

624
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:32,400
I can wait for you.

625
00:31:33,480 --> 00:31:34,800
I'm going to be here a long time.

626
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:36,400
Don't wait up for me.

627
00:31:38,039 --> 00:31:41,319
I'm giving you one last chance.

628
00:31:42,599 --> 00:31:43,599
Please, just go.

629
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:49,640
This is the path I chose.

630
00:31:49,720 --> 00:31:52,279
No matter how hard it gets,
I'm going to see it through.

631
00:31:53,759 --> 00:31:55,136
I just want to do my job
and make an honest living.

632
00:31:55,160 --> 00:31:56,280
I hope you can respect that.

633
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:29,239
Mr. Pao Bei.

634
00:32:29,319 --> 00:32:30,039
Boss P'Aya

635
00:32:30,119 --> 00:32:32,360
asked me to bring you some
professional protective gear.

636
00:32:32,440 --> 00:32:34,360
Here's an N95 respirator,

637
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:36,575
along with heavy-duty nitrile
gloves and a hazmat suit.

638
00:32:36,599 --> 00:32:38,239
Boss P'Aya specifically mentioned

639
00:32:38,319 --> 00:32:39,400
that some of the lab waste

640
00:32:39,480 --> 00:32:41,239
contains unneutralized chemicals.

641
00:32:41,319 --> 00:32:42,399
Standard gear won't cut it.

642
00:32:43,559 --> 00:32:44,799
Please thank Boss P'Aya for me.

643
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:48,095
And thanks for coming
all the way down here.

644
00:32:48,119 --> 00:32:48,920
Just doing my job.

645
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:50,320
Make sure you actually wear them.

646
00:32:50,839 --> 00:32:51,839
Safety first.

647
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:54,759
Are you feeling okay?

648
00:32:54,839 --> 00:32:56,400
You look a little pale.

649
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:58,800
It's nothing.

650
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:00,720
I've just been a bit
under the weather lately.

651
00:33:01,759 --> 00:33:04,400
I was supposed to deliver
these files to Boss P'Aya,

652
00:33:04,480 --> 00:33:05,960
but halfway here...

653
00:33:07,319 --> 00:33:09,080
You're carrying all these files?

654
00:33:09,160 --> 00:33:10,999
That's way too much for you right now.

655
00:33:11,079 --> 00:33:12,279
Why don't I take them for you?

656
00:33:13,000 --> 00:33:16,039
I can't. These are strictly confidential.

657
00:33:16,119 --> 00:33:17,279
Per company protocol,

658
00:33:17,359 --> 00:33:18,839
I have to deliver them in person.

659
00:33:20,519 --> 00:33:21,680
Well,

660
00:33:22,759 --> 00:33:23,239
how about this?

661
00:33:23,319 --> 00:33:24,519
I'll walk over there with you.

662
00:33:24,599 --> 00:33:25,400
You hold on to the files,

663
00:33:25,480 --> 00:33:26,199
and I'll help support you.

664
00:33:26,279 --> 00:33:28,599
Thank you so much. I really appreciate it.

665
00:33:36,200 --> 00:33:37,200
Let's go.

666
00:33:52,039 --> 00:33:52,800
Uh-oh.

667
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:54,055
I really need to use the restroom.

668
00:33:54,079 --> 00:33:55,839
Hold these for a
second, I'll be right back.

669
00:34:02,680 --> 00:34:03,560
Mr. Wang,

670
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,400
we need to speed things up

671
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:07,160
with the new training base in Chiang Saen.

672
00:34:07,640 --> 00:34:08,840
Right.

673
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:10,215
Background checks must be thorough,

674
00:34:10,239 --> 00:34:11,840
especially the psych evaluations.

675
00:34:11,920 --> 00:34:13,720
I want the full stress-test data

676
00:34:13,800 --> 00:34:14,920
and their compliance scores.

677
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:16,800
Keep the digital backups at your base,

678
00:34:16,880 --> 00:34:17,936
and send the copies directly to me.

679
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:19,079
Training base?

680
00:34:19,159 --> 00:34:20,159
Trainees?

681
00:34:20,239 --> 00:34:21,639
Psych evaluations?

682
00:34:21,719 --> 00:34:23,400
Compliance scores?

683
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:25,480
This doesn't sound like
normal talent training.

684
00:34:26,320 --> 00:34:28,840
It sounds more like some kind
of extreme screening process.

685
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:31,800
Is Jinding the name of a company?

686
00:34:46,039 --> 00:34:46,599
I'm so sorry

687
00:34:46,679 --> 00:34:47,760
for keeping you waiting.

688
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:51,559
If you're good now, I'll head back.

689
00:34:51,639 --> 00:34:53,479
Take it easy, and make
sure you get some rest.

690
00:34:53,880 --> 00:34:54,880
Right.

691
00:34:56,920 --> 00:35:00,000
I don't want any data leaks whatsoever.

692
00:35:02,519 --> 00:35:04,159
Good. Leave it at that.

693
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:16,119
That doesn't sound like
grooming artists at all.

694
00:35:16,199 --> 00:35:17,360
It sounds more like...

695
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:19,079
Wait a second.

696
00:35:19,159 --> 00:35:20,559
Milan mentioned before

697
00:35:20,639 --> 00:35:22,839
that his boss forced him
to do things against his will.

698
00:35:23,559 --> 00:35:26,159
Could it be tied to this company?

699
00:35:26,880 --> 00:35:28,039
Whatever.

700
00:35:28,119 --> 00:35:30,599
I'll hold on to this evidence
for now and figure it out later.

701
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:34,000
As outlined clearly on
the last page of our report,

702
00:35:34,039 --> 00:35:36,599
all our products tie
directly into this show.

703
00:35:37,159 --> 00:35:41,400
So this segment is definitely
going to be the main highlight.

704
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,680
To be honest, though,

705
00:35:43,760 --> 00:35:46,000
several guests we approached
are having second thoughts.

706
00:35:46,440 --> 00:35:49,439
We're going to need some
concrete feedback from the team here.

707
00:35:49,519 --> 00:35:51,015
We have to strike a balance
between creating good TV

708
00:35:51,039 --> 00:35:52,559
and keeping our guests safe.

709
00:35:52,639 --> 00:35:53,639
That's the top priority.

710
00:35:55,320 --> 00:35:56,439
We need someone

711
00:35:56,519 --> 00:35:58,679
to handle this initial taste test,

712
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:03,079
to provide professional notes for improvement,
and to have the entire process filmed.

713
00:36:14,159 --> 00:36:16,559
Manager, let me give it a shot.

714
00:36:17,519 --> 00:36:18,519
Pao Bei,

715
00:36:19,079 --> 00:36:22,280
these samples might be way
more intense than you expect.

716
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:24,679
Are you sure you want to do this?

717
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:27,479
Understanding product characteristics

718
00:36:27,559 --> 00:36:29,599
is a crucial part of product
development anyway.

719
00:36:29,679 --> 00:36:30,679
True.

720
00:36:30,719 --> 00:36:34,159
Besides, I personally
enjoy a good challenge.

721
00:36:36,280 --> 00:36:37,560
Well, since we have a volunteer,

722
00:36:38,639 --> 00:36:39,800
let's lock it in.

723
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:40,880
Sounds good.

724
00:37:56,360 --> 00:37:58,119
Boss P'Eng, are you okay with this?

725
00:37:58,199 --> 00:37:59,199
Fine.

726
00:38:18,840 --> 00:38:20,920
If it's out of your league,

727
00:38:21,840 --> 00:38:22,959
don't try to play tough.

728
00:38:23,039 --> 00:38:24,279
We can always get someone else.

729
00:38:32,199 --> 00:38:33,639
Quite a crowd in here today.

730
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:38,079
Running the preliminary
tests for the flavor challenge?

731
00:38:43,960 --> 00:38:46,039
Doesn't he look a bit unwell?

732
00:38:50,199 --> 00:38:50,840
Boss P'Aya,

733
00:38:50,920 --> 00:38:52,200
perfect timing.

734
00:38:52,280 --> 00:38:53,680
We're doing a dry run for the show.

735
00:38:53,760 --> 00:38:55,800
This is Pao Bei, our new team member.

736
00:38:55,880 --> 00:38:57,119
He's incredibly dedicated.

737
00:38:57,920 --> 00:39:00,200
He's personally testing every single one

738
00:39:00,280 --> 00:39:01,559
of our pending samples.

739
00:39:13,239 --> 00:39:15,280
This kind of extreme sensory test

740
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:16,999
takes a massive toll on the body.

741
00:39:17,079 --> 00:39:18,800
One person shouldn't be taking it all on.

742
00:39:19,519 --> 00:39:22,119
I think we should wrap up today's testing.

743
00:39:22,199 --> 00:39:24,880
Split the rest among the team,

744
00:39:25,599 --> 00:39:27,519
or use lab equipment to assist.

745
00:39:27,599 --> 00:39:29,359
You'll get more accurate
data that way, too.

746
00:39:30,719 --> 00:39:32,800
Nobody twisted his arm.

747
00:39:32,880 --> 00:39:35,039
He raised his own hand and volunteered.

748
00:39:36,440 --> 00:39:37,816
Thank you for your concern, Boss P'Aya.

749
00:39:37,840 --> 00:39:39,240
I'm fine, really.

750
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:40,320
It's...

751
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:42,320
It's just part of my job.

752
00:39:44,960 --> 00:39:47,880
Besides, only by experiencing it firsthand

753
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:49,840
can I give the most
honest, useful feedback.

754
00:39:51,320 --> 00:39:52,800
Please, let me finish.

755
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:56,800
Just make sure you know your limits.

756
00:39:56,880 --> 00:39:58,239
Don't push yourself too hard.

757
00:39:58,760 --> 00:40:00,159
Your health comes first.

758
00:40:51,480 --> 00:40:52,559
Manager,

759
00:40:52,639 --> 00:40:54,159
Director.

760
00:40:54,679 --> 00:40:59,959
The initial sensory test
for all samples is complete.

761
00:41:00,039 --> 00:41:02,400
I suggest keeping

762
00:41:04,079 --> 00:41:08,199
cold milk and club soda on set.

763
00:41:09,719 --> 00:41:13,280
It'll really help soothe
the burn for the guests.

764
00:41:17,360 --> 00:41:19,679
Just my two cents...

765
00:41:27,599 --> 00:41:29,199
Good work, Pao Bei.

766
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:48,000
Pao Bei!

767
00:41:50,199 --> 00:41:51,199
Pao Bei!

768
00:41:52,320 --> 00:41:53,320
Pao Bei!

769
00:41:53,400 --> 00:41:54,840
Wake up, Pao Bei!

770
00:42:00,760 --> 00:42:02,159
Doctor,

771
00:42:02,239 --> 00:42:03,159
in his condition,

772
00:42:03,239 --> 00:42:04,535
are you sure we don't
need to get him to a hospital

773
00:42:04,559 --> 00:42:05,559
for a full checkup?

774
00:42:06,159 --> 00:42:07,920
Judging by his current vitals,

775
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:10,760
he likely passed out
from acute gastroenteritis.

776
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:12,240
No need to move him just yet.

777
00:42:12,320 --> 00:42:14,080
Let's put him on an IV
drip and monitor him.

778
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:16,599
Once he wakes up,

779
00:42:16,679 --> 00:42:19,440
if the symptoms persist,
we can take him in then.

780
00:42:20,800 --> 00:42:22,760
I'll have someone prep the IV.

781
00:42:24,119 --> 00:42:25,360
Thank you, Dr. Liu.

782
00:42:31,840 --> 00:42:32,840
I'm sorry, Boss P'Eng.

783
00:42:33,400 --> 00:42:34,440
This is entirely my fault.

784
00:42:34,480 --> 00:42:35,159
I shouldn't have...

785
00:42:35,239 --> 00:42:36,439
It has nothing to do with you.

786
00:42:37,719 --> 00:42:38,760
It was just for the show.

787
00:42:39,400 --> 00:42:40,920
His body just couldn't handle it.

788
00:42:41,599 --> 00:42:44,320
So, about the blind taste test segment...

789
00:42:44,400 --> 00:42:45,400
Keep it.

790
00:42:45,480 --> 00:42:47,320
The issue lies with his
own weak constitution.

791
00:42:47,679 --> 00:42:50,880
Take the feedback and notes he logged,

792
00:42:50,960 --> 00:42:53,599
and work with the product
team to tweak the formula.

793
00:42:53,679 --> 00:42:56,000
Just make sure the guests
are safe during filming.

794
00:42:58,239 --> 00:42:59,239
Right.

795
00:43:05,880 --> 00:43:07,119
Understood.

796
00:43:09,800 --> 00:43:10,800
Sir.

797
00:43:13,360 --> 00:43:15,400
Get the car ready. I'm
heading over right now.

798
00:43:15,480 --> 00:43:16,480
Yes, sir.

799
00:43:23,960 --> 00:43:26,199
Stay here and keep an eye on him for me.

800
00:43:27,079 --> 00:43:28,079
Sir,

801
00:43:29,360 --> 00:43:31,760
if you're going alone,
please keep a cool head.

802
00:43:31,840 --> 00:43:33,039
Don't do anything rash.

803
00:43:33,119 --> 00:43:34,959
The bodyguards are
already waiting downstairs.

804
00:43:35,159 --> 00:43:35,959
Unless you have no other choice,

805
00:43:36,039 --> 00:43:36,599
please don't...

806
00:43:36,679 --> 00:43:38,079
Relax.

807
00:43:38,159 --> 00:43:39,159
I know what I'm doing.

808
00:43:45,719 --> 00:43:46,776
Which VIP room are they in?

809
00:43:46,800 --> 00:43:48,559
Room 888, just up ahead.

810
00:43:48,639 --> 00:43:51,079
Looks like there are some
guests from Huabo in there, too.

811
00:43:51,800 --> 00:43:53,119
Guests from Huabo?

812
00:43:53,920 --> 00:43:55,039
Talent agents?

813
00:43:55,559 --> 00:43:57,320
I wouldn't know about that, sir.

814
00:43:57,400 --> 00:43:59,960
I just heard they're some
big shots from Huabo.

815
00:44:06,800 --> 00:44:07,800
Hello, A Pong.

816
00:44:08,559 --> 00:44:09,320
Get over here.

817
00:44:09,400 --> 00:44:10,400
I need you.

818
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:16,960
Good. Now I can take them all down at once.
